# wiki-docs CI gate (do not skip)

CI job `wiki-docs` fails a PR whose body has no valid `## Documentation impact` section. Before opening a PR, editing its body or saying it is ready:

1. Check whether the diff touches `docs/wiki/`.
2. Under `## Documentation impact`, check **exactly one** of `- [x] Wiki updated` / `- [x] No Wiki update needed - <specific reason>`, and keep the other line present and unchecked.
3. After fixing only the body, push a new commit: a re-run reuses the stale event body.

Full rules, the exact format and stacked PRs: [standards/docs-and-wiki.md](../../standards/docs-and-wiki.md).
